# 6️⃣ Reverse an Array

### 📌 Problem

Print:

```java
{10, 20, 30, 40, 50}
```

in reverse order.

### 💻 Code

```java
package p1;

public class ReverseAnArray {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] arr = {10, 20, 30, 40, 50};

        System.out.print("Reverse Array = ");

        for (int i = arr.length - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
            System.out.print(arr[i] + " ");
        }
    }
}
```

### 📤 Output

```text
Reverse Array = 50 40 30 20 10
```

### 🧠 Array Indexes

```text
Value:  10   20   30   40   50
Index:   0    1    2    3    4
```

For reverse:

```text
4 → 3 → 2 → 1 → 0
```

### ⭐ Important Pattern

```java
for (int i = arr.length - 1; i >= 0; i--)
```

This means:

* Start at last index.
* Continue while `i >= 0`.
* Decrease `i` using `i--`.

### ⏱️ Complexity

```text
Time:  O(n)
Space: O(1)
```

