# 🔟 Second Largest Element

### 📌 Problem

Find the second-largest element without sorting.

Array:

```java
{10, 25, 7, 40, 15}
```

Expected:

```text
25
```

### 💻 Code

```java
package p1;

public class SecondLargest {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int[] arr = {10, 25, 7, 40, 15};

        int largest = arr[0];
        int secondLargest = largest;

        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {

            if (arr[i] > largest) {

                secondLargest = largest;
                largest = arr[i];
            }
        }

        System.out.println("Second Largest = " + secondLargest);
    }
}
```

### 📤 Output

```text
Second Largest = 25
```

### 🧠 Important Concept

When a **new largest** is found:

```text
Old largest → second largest
New value   → largest
```

Example:

```text
largest = 25
secondLargest = 10

Find 40

secondLargest = 25
largest = 40
```

### ⭐ Important Order

Correct:

```java
secondLargest = largest;
largest = arr[i];
```

Not:

```java
largest = arr[i];
secondLargest = arr[i];
```

because then both could become the same value.

### ⚠️ Interview Note

This basic version works for the simple example we practiced, but a production/interview-ready implementation should also handle edge cases such as:

* Arrays with fewer than 2 elements
* Duplicate largest values
* Negative numbers
* Whether "second largest" means distinct second largest

We'll revisit this problem later with those cases.

